{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"b6664132c18a808bfecc39bb7251df084f29c69fb4e58bd238f7019345b5fe0c","slug":"index","location":"/intro.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"From Models to Learning","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Pierre-Luc Bacon","given":"Pierre-Luc","family":"Bacon"},"name":"Pierre-Luc Bacon","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/pierrelux/rlbook","math":{"\\Proj":{"macro":"\\mathsf{P}"},"\\Residual":{"macro":"\\mathsf{N}"},"\\Contraction":{"macro":"\\mathsf{T}"},"\\Bellman":{"macro":"\\mathsf{L}"},"\\BellmanPi":{"macro":"\\mathsf{L}_\\pi"},"\\BellmanQuad":{"macro":"\\widetilde{\\mathsf{L}}"},"\\EulerResidual":{"macro":"\\mathsf{H}"},"\\Policy":{"macro":"\\pi"}},"source_url":"https://github.com/pierrelux/rlbook/blob/main/intro.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/pierrelux/rlbook/edit/main/intro.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"intro.md","url":"/rlbook/build/intro-6bb16836ad6f96925ac0d8dca68fdb51.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reinforcement learning studies decisions whose consequences unfold over time.\nBefore an algorithm can learn, someone must decide what the system is, which\nquantities form its state, which actions are available, what can be observed,\nand how success is measured. In benchmark environments these choices have\nalready been made. In applications they are often the hardest part of the work.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"OrEiPBMRzc"}],"key":"fpDk2ftmCl"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sensors are noisy, constraints are non-negotiable, and objectives may conflict.\nA controller that performs well in a simulator can fail because the simulator\npermits an impossible force or omits a mode transition. A learned policy can\noptimize the reward it was given while violating a requirement that never\nentered the model. These are failures of formulation rather than failures of a\nparticular reinforcement-learning algorithm.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"A0A3UwbDz0"}],"key":"waM82p03Oj"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":23,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same issue appears across several communities. Control theory, dynamic\nprogramming, operations research, economics, and reinforcement learning use\ndifferent vocabularies, but each asks how actions change future outcomes. In\ndeployed optimization systems, learned predictors often sit inside explicit\nobjectives and constraints. Ride matching and robot control provide examples at\nlarge scale ","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"Rk3puDOERS"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","children":[{"type":"cite","kind":"parenthetical","label":"Uber2025","identifier":"uber2025","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uber AI Labs, 2025","key":"FGQe1Qc0DD"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"tLFuiul4Xd"},{"type":"cite","kind":"parenthetical","label":"ANYbotics2023","identifier":"anybotics2023","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ANYbotics, 2023","key":"T1rdnxBmjs"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"Xau78kXajf"}],"key":"Ci39PP73ar"},{"type":"text","value":", while applied work more generally\nfaces the difficulty of learning both the objective and the environment\n","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"GEnmrskPb6"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","children":[{"type":"cite","kind":"parenthetical","label":"Iskhakov2020","identifier":"iskhakov2020","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Iskhakov ","key":"Lc4fow4wFd"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"et al.","key":"Kq2qdxI612"}],"key":"FU8oi2YlvQ"},{"type":"text","value":", 2020","key":"hc7Z4pQ3ns"}],"enumerator":"3","key":"MajbdT5Arr"}],"key":"IErlBDZkdZ"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"vgoU8a20Xd"}],"key":"NsUisVhP7u"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Decision Problem","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"USPZS7YiDe"}],"identifier":"the-decision-problem","label":"The Decision Problem","html_id":"the-decision-problem","implicit":true,"key":"WR8ihoFnVJ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The term ","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"Zau3j72fzO"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"reinforcement learning","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"r2TTY30fph"}],"key":"BsneQl9e6P"},{"type":"text","value":" can name a problem, a family of algorithms,\nor a research community. This book uses it first as a decision problem: an\nagent receives information, chooses actions, and experiences consequences. That\ndescription includes model predictive control, dynamic programming, direct\npolicy search, and many systems that are not usually labeled as RL.","position":{"start":{"line":27,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"key":"nSmlPvl56H"}],"key":"RYf4ziSce6"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":34,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The problem is rarely handed to us in finished form. A useful formulation must\nanswer five questions:","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"DlaXSrqYiP"}],"key":"K0zjM8bYCh"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which variables summarize the information needed for future decisions?","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"TNiDrshtjt"}],"key":"aq8zRkkGpj"}],"key":"WufxdbFZc7"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which actions can the decision maker actually apply?","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"CuIMlVRGYM"}],"key":"pbgo7UbGUE"}],"key":"noH8cKAX6K"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How do actions, disturbances, and uncertainty change the system?","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"Z6IHh8tCWe"}],"key":"NyzRmMftxN"}],"key":"BxHpPw8DLH"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which outcomes should the objective reward or penalize?","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"gawEZhVqqL"}],"key":"uq91a6o6wi"}],"key":"cKw5l2sh6O"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which physical, operational, or safety constraints must always hold?","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"I3ssKbQO4J"}],"key":"D8qQicMAum"}],"key":"WD4hFFTNHf"}],"key":"cw941gpNKT"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The answers determine which computations are available. An explicit\ndifferential equation can expose derivatives and conservation laws. A simulator\nmay provide only trajectory samples. Logged data cannot answer arbitrary\ncounterfactual queries without additional assumptions. Interaction provides new\ndata, but it also consumes time and can damage the system.","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"ATX0R6Bbbh"}],"key":"JI9F3MhmuX"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Book’s Progression","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"RqAwu3l8CM"}],"identifier":"the-books-progression","label":"The Book’s Progression","html_id":"the-books-progression","implicit":true,"key":"cBQIP7Q0b3"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The technical development follows the information available about the decision\nproblem. It begins with models because every later method consumes a model\ninterface, even when that interface consists only of sampled transitions.","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"ytDiCbWeS3"}],"key":"CyqYxCqeSC"},{"type":"table","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableRow","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableCell","header":true,"position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Part","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"wWEvCPjO1W"}],"key":"qEfq7hQtUN"},{"type":"tableCell","header":true,"position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Question","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"azauWMqpyU"}],"key":"INMeqn0Q4Z"},{"type":"tableCell","header":true,"position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"MOi2BqjPBU"}],"key":"v3uRQoQHLX"}],"key":"LEsnMAL8ox"},{"type":"tableRow","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modeling","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"pw6S7im6XQ"}],"key":"t7tw3w11b2"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"What evolves, what can be observed, and where does an action enter?","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"bP9RnuHapf"}],"key":"fPiA1xCdZo"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A state, action, disturbance, objective, constraint set, and model interface","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"LFVqXgsuIu"}],"key":"wOJTYYD6e9"}],"key":"RHM2vouYXa"},{"type":"tableRow","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trajectory optimization","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"qAWzUNV0wF"}],"key":"e7BzhKo2Hc"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"What action sequence performs well from one initial condition?","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"BH8HxRe4Py"}],"key":"zEUQ74KKpP"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"An open-loop plan","position":{"start":{"line":57,"column":1},"end":{"line":57,"column":1}},"key":"z39msCdKcA"}],"key":"Tj0LF49JyI"}],"key":"QA83CyyRd8"},{"type":"tableRow","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model predictive control","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"Wl42OedjYO"}],"key":"anDhoms991"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"How can the plan react to new measurements?","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"hkVRphqhg1"}],"key":"UPi0GqUdHg"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Feedback through repeated replanning","position":{"start":{"line":58,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"key":"RZvwYONC94"}],"key":"qWasq9nWaI"}],"key":"Mcq0JeF6kf"},{"type":"tableRow","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic programming","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"JiAUBjYxTP"}],"key":"hF8gJL5QEW"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"How can decisions be optimized for many possible future states?","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"TgTRPmaDz4"}],"key":"i5b65rXNZn"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A value function and state-contingent policy","position":{"start":{"line":59,"column":1},"end":{"line":59,"column":1}},"key":"RtaSkJRHJo"}],"key":"HH9Ekrr2vB"}],"key":"fNm2z3Y5Z6"},{"type":"tableRow","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Approximation and learning","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"oa4Ehn8qHf"}],"key":"DTJLcSzdcw"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which required object is unavailable or too expensive to compute exactly?","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"upGBHgHVmc"}],"key":"aiyPenweF3"},{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"An approximation learned from models, samples, or interaction","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"IobhJOMwUD"}],"key":"c3JjIflXpt"}],"key":"MoCij16Yzh"}],"key":"jZHjvqbN5l"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This order does not assume that a complete mechanistic model is always\navailable. It makes the information restriction explicit. Known conservation\nlaws, geometry, and constraints remain in the formulation; uncertain\nparameters, residual dynamics, value functions, or policies become learning\ntargets. Black-box neural networks enter as components when their flexibility\nmatches the uncertain part of the problem.","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"ikQRay3wVb"}],"key":"bY5KEW135s"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The chapters repeatedly test this distinction on concrete systems. A\nplayground swing exposes internal actuation and an omitted slack-chain mode. A\ncart-pole separates global trajectory planning from local stabilization. An\noverhead crane and a wave-energy converter show how actuator geometry and hard\nconstraints shape optimization. The examples are intentionally different: the\nmethod should follow from the structure of the problem, rather than from a\npreferred benchmark.","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"XMeuXvXvWa"}],"key":"T3SutJ7bZD"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The goal is not to survey every technique superficially. It is to go deep on the mathematical foundations that are shared across methods: dynamic programming, function approximation, optimization, and the interplay between them. These structures recur throughout sequential decision-making, whether in reinforcement learning, control theory, or operations research. Master them once, and you can recognize them in different guises.","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"vslsvEwu7u"}],"key":"tg3O9MAnsc"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Self-checks","position":{"start":{"line":79,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"key":"V1FiDRD0NK"}],"identifier":"self-checks","label":"Self-checks","html_id":"self-checks","implicit":true,"key":"usN8dTt4PY"},{"type":"exercise","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Problem before algorithm","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"Byd5SzwRih"}],"key":"Ajy9KfgzSe"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A production controller must respect a hard storage limit. Is selecting a learning algorithm enough to define the reinforcement-learning problem? Name two pieces of structure that must be specified first.","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"key":"RPGoorFDzP"}],"key":"RDt4B5fHd8"}],"label":"ex-intro-check-1","identifier":"ex-intro-check-1","enumerated":true,"enumerator":"1","html_id":"ex-intro-check-1","key":"WjPAnp8mAk"},{"type":"solution","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solution to ","key":"ZIZvCysQa3"},{"type":"crossReference","label":"ex-intro-check-1","identifier":"ex-intro-check-1","kind":"exercise","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exercise ","key":"O2jqLW1LQK"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"ZDCZjWe8nZ"}],"template":"Exercise %s","enumerator":"1","resolved":true,"html_id":"ex-intro-check-1","key":"sRVFwWUR6a"}],"key":"bWR2WfHH7v"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":90,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"No. At minimum, the state and available decisions must be defined, together with the objective and the hard storage constraint. The transition or feedback structure must also say how decisions affect future states.","position":{"start":{"line":90,"column":1},"end":{"line":90,"column":1}},"key":"sxRasJdWq4"}],"key":"iWMWlwbrdo"}],"class":"dropdown","key":"vUzhaNqj5V"},{"type":"exercise","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared structure","position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"key":"L1ur9iXW2Q"}],"key":"w9OM7pKSYn"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"What feature makes trajectory optimization, model predictive control, and reinforcement learning members of the same decision-making family?","position":{"start":{"line":96,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"key":"SzxIGBIQK3"}],"key":"FIyQCTEldK"}],"label":"ex-intro-check-2","identifier":"ex-intro-check-2","enumerated":true,"enumerator":"2","html_id":"ex-intro-check-2","key":"zoTOrk449p"},{"type":"solution","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solution to ","key":"QMtKhGlXco"},{"type":"crossReference","label":"ex-intro-check-2","identifier":"ex-intro-check-2","kind":"exercise","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exercise ","key":"iMp7DViOk4"},{"type":"text","value":"2","key":"LHzFvOyAXm"}],"template":"Exercise %s","enumerator":"2","resolved":true,"html_id":"ex-intro-check-2","key":"ppkTMQ8IdI"}],"key":"AWquU3Ng0U"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"All three choose actions whose consequences unfold through a dynamical system over time, so present decisions must account for future objectives and constraints.","position":{"start":{"line":102,"column":1},"end":{"line":102,"column":1}},"key":"ldRjEkz7kh"}],"key":"Y1qn6gPriB"}],"class":"dropdown","key":"VOfm7KVly9"}],"key":"esvB0APfNh"}],"key":"R9jQmer9qe"},"references":{"cite":{"order":["Uber2025","ANYbotics2023","Iskhakov2020"],"data":{"Uber2025":{"label":"Uber2025","enumerator":"1","html":"Uber AI Labs. (2025). <i>Reinforcement Learning at Scale for Ride-Matching Optimization</i>. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.uber.com/blog/rl-ride-matching\">https://www.uber.com/blog/rl-ride-matching</a>","url":"https://www.uber.com/blog/rl-ride-matching"},"ANYbotics2023":{"label":"ANYbotics2023","enumerator":"2","html":"ANYbotics. (2023). <i>ANYmal: RL-Powered Autonomous Inspection</i>. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.anybotics.com/anymal-inspection\">https://www.anybotics.com/anymal-inspection</a>","url":"https://www.anybotics.com/anymal-inspection"},"Iskhakov2020":{"label":"Iskhakov2020","enumerator":"3","doi":"10.1093/ectj/utaa019","html":"Iskhakov, F., Rust, J., & Schjerning, B. (2020). Machine learning and structural econometrics: contrasts and synergies. <i>The Econometrics Journal</i>, <i>23</i>(3), S81–S124. <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1093/ectj/utaa019\">10.1093/ectj/utaa019</a>","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ectj/utaa019"}}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"next":{"title":"Syllabus · Plan de cours","url":"/syllabus","group":"Building Up RL: From Dynamics and Control to Learning"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}